+# The complete court attachment has 531 identifier rows, not a demonstrated 531 specimens
+
+October 29, 2026. Steel preservation/custody track; existing B188/H005, AUD011/AUD016 and STL01–STL04. This completes a previously unperformed accounting of the **nine-page July 2010 Exhibit A** held in a public municipal agenda packet. It supplies a reproducible row ledger, not the missing native inventory, transfer history or building-attribution rationale.
+
+## Source and exact reading scope
+
+The [December 13, 2010 Clearwater agenda packet](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/edoc/243567/12132010.pdf?dbid=0&repo=Clearwater) contains 533 physical PDF pages and 61,333,079 bytes. SHA-256: **f2696cfeab6ca20d807923afbe9c0c8ad86e13612b56aa2bc2a64311f8dd1a75**. The source was acquired October 29, 2026; this unit rechecked its bytes, hash and page count without modifying it. The attachment's displayed court header is Case **1:21-mc-00097-AKH-THK**, Document **1509**, Filed **07/22/2010**. Physical PDF pages **69–77** are printed Exhibit A pages **1–9**. Page locators refer to this municipal packet, not another copy's pagination.
+
+All nine identifier columns, their table boundaries and adjacent descriptions were visually inspected in this unit. Every accepted identifier is recorded in [IDENTIFIER-ROWS.json](IDENTIFIER-ROWS.json), retaining leading zeros, order and repeated entries. The row ordinals are supplied research locators, not extra numbers printed on the source. No blank or multiline identifier rows were observed. No identifier remained unresolved in this reading; a native list or independent reading could still reveal a transcription error.
+
+The [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/4b57a56d460bd7ea4b34e9f8771cf5f472d19250/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-clearwater-agreement-2026-10-29/README.md) had read the nine pages but transcribed only the **104 NIST-prefixed entries** on the last two. Those 104 entries were checked again by position and exact string and match the earlier transcription. This is a same-source, same-agent check, not independent corroboration. The new work accounts for the other 427 rows and the complete list's counting units.
+
+## Reproducible results
+
+| Measure | Result | What it counts |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Identifier-bearing rows | **531** | Table entries in this copy of Exhibit A |
+| Distinct exact identifier strings | **530** | Unique strings, with no alias normalization |
+| Rows on physical pages 69–76 | **61 per page** | Eight visually inspected table pages |
+| Rows on physical page 77 | **43** | Final table page |
+| NIST-prefixed rows | **104** | An administrative label subset, not authenticated NIST specimen IDs |
+| Other-prefixed rows | **427** | The remaining entries, including the repeated label |
+
+Prefix counts are A 32; B 20; C 39; D 2; F 5; G 98; H 91; I 102; J 8; L 20; M 10; NIST 104. These are literal label-prefix counts, not independently established material categories. [COUNT-RESULTS.json](COUNT-RESULTS.json) and [verify_rows.py](verify_rows.py) preserve the arithmetic. The page totals follow the actual row readings; they were not generated by assuming a fixed number of rows per page.
+
+**G-0086 occurs twice:** physical page **71**, printed page **3**, identifier rows **25 and 26**; global ledger rows **147 and 148**. Both adjacent source descriptions read Steel Plate. This previously observed repetition is retained in both rows; the new complete-list check finds no other exact repeated identifier. It does not determine whether these entries describe one object, two objects, a transcription error or some other catalog convention. The reason remains TODO. A repeated identifier is not automatically a duplicate physical object or proof of careless or improper disposal.
+
+## The source shows why a row is not necessarily a specimen
+
+Selected visible descriptions provide specific counterexamples to one-row/one-steel-specimen accounting:
+
+- **NIST-068:** physical 76, row 24, describes two beams; **NIST-076**, same page row 30, describes three columns. **NIST-119**, same page row 52, describes a washer and nut.
+- **B-0068:** physical 69, row 52, describes granite; **F-0001**, physical 70 row 33, describes a reinforced-concrete column; **D-0001**, physical 70 row 31, describes a PATH train car.
+- **NIST-085:** physical 76, row 38, describes aluminum sheathing. The NIST prefix therefore cannot itself be treated as a material-composition finding. **L-0017**, physical 75 row 43, also describes aluminum with cutouts.
+
+[SELECTED-DESCRIPTORS.json](SELECTED-DESCRIPTORS.json) preserves the exact selected strings and row locators. These examples are not a full transcription or quantitative classification of all descriptions. They do not establish each object's composition by testing, present location, condition or original building.
+
+Preserve **531 rows, 530 strings, 104 NIST-prefixed rows, the separately reported 236 NIST samples and approximately 230 returned items** as differently scoped observations. This unit does not subtract one from another to manufacture missing-piece numbers. The actual object/assembly/coupon/alias, date, selection and custody crosswalk is missing. Nor does the presence of surviving entries establish that every useful specimen survived, that transfers occurred as authorized, or that scientific access was actually exercised.
+
+## Method and limits
+
+The original was rendered at 220 dpi with Poppler. Local Tesseract text/TSV outputs were used only as candidate/navigation aids. An exact-pattern OCR diagnostic missed or misread identifiers on every page, so OCR results were not silently substituted for the visual ledger. Raw OCR, page images, acquisition receipts and the original remain preserved locally on the verified media store. Nothing was inferred behind redactions or extracted from hidden text.
+
+This is a municipal-hosted court-copy representation. The scan/header/hash do not authenticate a native signed court file, January 2007 inventory, historical database, shipment, receipt or today's legal rights. The original order/agreements and their qualifications remain in the preceding review. This unit does not newly reread every earlier order or all 533 agenda pages. It performs no specimen testing, source repair, material-loss inference or adjudication of motive, misconduct or conspiracy.
+
+The strongest limitation is that arithmetic from a manual transcription is only as good as the reading and source copy. All nine pages were checked, and the earlier 104-row subset matches, but an independent reader and native inventory could change individual readings or explain row/object relationships. They are concrete next controls, not tests already completed.
+
+## Remaining original-record work
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains STL01–STL04: original preservation decisions; native inventory/alias and transfer history; W14A/W14B/C12/Sample 1 attribution rationale and coupon links; WJE selection/review/delivery records. The duplicate-label reason, complete native list/version and object-level crosswalk are additional precise retrieval targets. The December 2009 order and its actual attached list remain unacquired; a docket description is not their text.
+
+All five original work-plan tracks remain open. FAA corrected-QFR/receipt and signed action/no-action/implementation records, telephone native carrier/operator joins, recorder installed-policy/clock/custody tests and materials matched-specimen/native-instrument joins remain separate dependencies. Existing technical results are not relabeled unperformed; this row census does not validate or replace them. A finished list count is not completion of the broader investigation.
+
+Only research notes, factual nonpersonal identifiers, selected public descriptions and verification code are included in this addition. Raw scans, unrelated agenda content, signatures, contacts, private case material and correspondence are excluded. Original bytes, earlier public findings and unresolved values remain unchanged. [REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json](REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json) records the checklist and actual checks; [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) records these additive notes against absence, rather than masquerading as a native-inventory change history.
